{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The wood screws were the closest match because they serve a fastening purpose, like the washers, nuts, and bolts I recently chose.",
    "That connection was only partial: I have shown more interest in assorted metric hardware than in one size of exterior wood screw."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Glue and wiring terminals can also join things, but they serve different tasks from the mechanical fastening and magnetic hanging items I recently selected.",
    "The air regulator, inspection camera, water regulator, and cutting discs require specific equipment or projects that my recent activity does not establish.",
    "A large worktable, gloves, and tubing do not address a clear current need, so I would pass rather than interact just because they might be useful someday."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My hardware purchases seemed to be taken as interest in a broad range of workshop supplies.",
    "The appeal of an assortment seemed to carry over to electrical connectors, even though having multiple sizes does not make an unrelated task relevant to me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent choices repeatedly involved magnetic hooks and small mechanical fasteners; their particular functions matter more than a general connection to tools or repairs.",
    "The metric sizes and assortment of my nuts, bolts, and locking washers matter when judging whether other fasteners would be useful.",
    "My hand-truck interaction was much older than the closely timed hook and fastener interactions, which give a clearer indication of my recent interests."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You partly recognized my interest in fastening supplies but stretched it into workshop and maintenance needs I have not shown."
}"}
